// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential DLL Sideloading of SPPC.dll
// Sigma ID: 5e7f8a4b-9c3d-4f2e-b1a6-8d7e9f0c2b3a
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-03-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading of SPPC.dll by identifying instances where the DLL is loaded
//   from a directory other than the legitimate Windows system directories.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate software that may load SPPC.dll from non-standard locations, baselining and further investigation required.
// References:
//   - https://hijacklibs.net/entries/microsoft/built-in/sppc.html
//   - https://arcticwolf.com/resources/blog/sloppylemming-deploys-burrowshell-and-rust-based-rat-to-target-pakistan-and-bangladesh/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/88613eedefe2a4c6caa63eaa3d150ce9449655b2/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_sppc.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\sppc.dll" and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\")))
